  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A cut and pegged board of grey timber faced with thin dressed stone on the wet side, used to hold and release water between two terrace basins. Boards are made to the basin rather than to any standard, and each carries the house mark on the dry face, low down, where it is under water for most of the year. This one warped along the grain and was pulled in 2288. The wear on the lifting notches runs left-handed for most of its life and right-handed at the end, a change the house attributes without hesitation to a quarrel and declines to describe further.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
